; STAGE INTRO: Particle-physics lab scene + transport-to-alien-world.
;
; Gameplay role: opening cinematic. Lester Chaykin arrives at his
; lab one stormy night to run an experiment with a particle
; accelerator. Lightning hits the building, the experiment goes
; haywire, and Lester is transported to the alien world. The stage
; ends with him appearing underwater in the LAKE pool.
;
; Branches that ship INTRO:
;   chahi_amiga_1991, dos_1992, cartridge_1992 (snes_eu, genesis_eu),
;   gba_2004 (foxy port).
;
; This is THE LONGEST cinematic in the game, and most ports use
; identical bytecode aside from EQU-table reordering. AWVM_Tools
; mislabels the cartridge/GBA INTRO chunk as "Code-wheel screen" —
; cartridges have no codewheel, so that label is a known artifact.
;
; The unified file is structured as 15 named chapter chunks
; (intro/intro_*.inc) — each chunk is a slice of byte-address space,
; NOT a sequential scene. **Include order is byte-order in the cart
; bytecode**, NOT runtime execution order. The first scene the player
; sees (the lab-particles intro) lives in the LAST chunk
; (`intro_scene_final.inc`) — the entry point in the FIRST chunk
; jumps forward to it via `setup channel=0x01, address=
; INTRO_SCENE_INIT_PARTICLES`.
;
; ## Execution model — multi-channel cooperative scheduler
;
; The AW VM has 64 channels; INTRO uses ~10 of them concurrently.
; There's no single "main" routine — instead, scenes are built from
; cooperating per-channel coroutines:
;
;   - Channel 0x3C runs the per-tick blit/dispatch loop
;     (`BLIT_AND_DISPATCH_HERO_ACTION` or `BLIT_AND_COPY_PAGE_FF_LOOP`).
;   - Channel 0x01 runs the foreground scene logic.
;   - Channel 0x02 runs the background-audio + walking-feet loop.
;   - Channel 0x03 runs the looping avatar/decor draw.
;   - Channels 0x06, 0x08, 0x09, 0x0A..0x0F are auxiliary (DNA helix
;     phases, particle phases, scene-transition wait loops).
;
; A "scene transition" is an opcode like:
;
;     setup channel=0x01, address=NEXT_SCENE_ROUTINE
;     setup channel=0x02, address=NEXT_AUDIO_ROUTINE
;     killChannel
;
; — the current channel kills itself, but before that it has wired
; the next phase onto its peer channels. This is why the chunks are
; not in execution order: the bytecode threads through them in a
; non-linear, multi-channel pattern.
;
; ## Within-routine scene flow
;
; Within a single channel's run, scenes flow as long sequential
; routines with `break`/`djnz` for timing:
;
;     mov [PAUSE_SLICES], N        ; how many ticks each `break` yields
;     mov [counter], M             ; frame count
;   FRAME_LOOP:
;     break                        ; yield to scheduler
;     djnz [counter], FRAME_LOOP   ; loop M*N ticks
;     <draw next frame>
;
; Music synchronisation uses the `MUS_MARK` variable: a music track
; sets the mark at each beat, and a channel can `wait until
; [MUS_MARK] == X` to gate the next phase on a music beat.
;
; ## Skip-intro / press-action handling
;
; The blit dispatch (`BLIT_AND_DISPATCH_HERO_ACTION`) checks
; `[HERO_ACTION]` each tick; if set, jumps to
; `INTRO_RESET_PAGES_AND_PAL_0` (in `intro_reset_and_lab_decor.inc`)
; which resets pages and replays from a known scene boundary. This
; is the "press a key to advance" mechanism players use to skip
; through the intro.
;
; Engine-managed special-purpose VM variables (HERO_POS_*, RANDOM_SEED, PAUSE_SLICES, etc.).
;@include "../_common_vars.inc"

; Cross-stage helper EQUs (LABEL_<HEX> / ADDR_AT_* placeholders shared between levels).
;@include "_helpers/_helpers_equ_aliases.inc"


	org 0x0000

; ============================================================
; Chapter chunks (in byte-address order, NOT execution order).
; ============================================================

; Bytecode entry point + per-tick blit dispatchers
; (BLIT_AND_DISPATCH_HERO_ACTION etc.). After loading resources and
; starting the music, the entry sets up channels 0x01/0x02/0x03/0x3C
; and kills itself — control then forwards to INTRO_SCENE_INIT_PARTICLES
; in `intro_scene_final.inc` (i.e. JUMPS to the LAST chunk for the
; INTRO level entry point + top-level scene dispatcher.
;@include "intro/intro_entry_and_dispatchers.inc"

; Mid-intro text-display routine (`INTRO_PAUSE_3_AND_DRAW_CIN_138`):
; draws CINEMATIC_138..143 + texts 0x190/0x191, then schedules
; `SCENE_TRANSITION_NEXT_PHASE` on channel 0x06 and
; `INTRO_TRANSITION_TO_LAKE_SCENE` on channel 0x02. Used at the
; INTRO first-scene init: pause + CIN_138 draw.
;@include "intro/intro_first_scene_init.inc"

; The 5-step linear scene-progression chain
; (`SCENE_TRANSITION_NEXT_PHASE` + `WAIT_INTRO_SCENE_1..5`). Each
; WAIT_INTRO_SCENE_N is reached by fall-through from the previous,
; waits N ticks, draws CINEMATIC_144 (background) + a foreground
; cinematic (145/146/147/CARKEY), and schedules
; `DRAW_CINEMATICS_166_TO_171` on channel 0x09. Drives the "car
; INTRO inter-scene transitions (SCENE_TRANSITION_NEXT_PHASE).
;@include "intro/intro_scene_transitions.inc"

; The DNA-helix logo animation (Another World / Out of This World
; opening identity). `SETUP_INTRO_DNA_CHANNELS` wires channels
; 0x0A/0x0B for the helix tick + draw loops; `DRAW_DNA_ANIMATION_LOOP`
; is the per-frame redraw. Includes
; `DRAW_CIN_035_PAL_3_REPEAT_HEAD` (target of a `jmp` from
; INTRO DNA-helix animation (SETUP_INTRO_DNA_CHANNELS / DNA_VAR_05 hold + drift loops + DRAW_CINEMATICS_166_171) followed by the lab-cinematic tail (DRAW_CIN_453_454_SEQ + DRAW_CIN_035_PAL_3_REPEAT_HEAD + DRAW_CIN_048_15_FRAMES_LOOP) that hands off to the next phase via setup-channel calls.
;@include "intro/intro_dna_animation.inc"

; Per-channel initialiser routines (`CH_0A_INIT_VAR_02`,
; `CH_0B_INIT_VAR_03`, ..., one per auxiliary channel). Each sets a
; counter variable to a starting value, then enters a wait-loop
; (`CH_0X_VAR_NN_WAIT_LOOP`). These are tick-driver coroutines for
; INTRO per-channel init helpers (CH_0A_INIT_VAR_02 et al.).
;@include "intro/intro_channel_inits.inc"

; Particle-effects driver (`SETUP_INTRO_PARTICLE_CHANNELS`,
; `PARTICLE_PHASE_350_FRAME_TIMER`, page-flip helpers
; `FILL_FF_PAGE_LOOP`/`SETUP_PAL19_AND_PAGE_FLIP`). Manages the
; lightning/electricity particles during the lab accident — a
; multi-channel storm of palette-19 flickers culminating in
; INTRO particle-channel setup (SETUP_INTRO_PARTICLE_CHANNELS).
;@include "intro/intro_particle_channels.inc"

; Reset-on-action handler (`INTRO_RESET_PAGES_AND_PAL_0`) — wakes up
; when `[HERO_ACTION] != 0` from the blit dispatcher. Replays the
; lab startup scene (`PLAY_FX_2C_AND_DRAW_CIN_000`,
; `DRAW_INTRO_DECOR_340`, `DRAW_INTRO_DECOR_337`) so the player can
; INTRO reset + lab decor (INTRO_RESET_PAGES_AND_PAL_0).
;@include "intro/intro_reset_and_lab_decor.inc"

; INTRO late-phase lab decor (DRAW_INTRO_DECOR_318 et al.).
;@include "intro/intro_lab_decor_late_phase.inc"

; Transition-to-LAKE scene assembly
; (`INTRO_TRANSITION_TO_LAKE_SETUP`,
; `PHASE_PAGE3_TO_0_PAL_16`, `INTRO_FILL_AND_DRAW_CIN_385`,
; `CITY_DRAW_411_412_LOOP`). Sets up the city panorama → particle
; vortex → underwater LAKE arrival pipeline. Note this is the
; "setup" half; the main animation happens in
; INTRO transition-to-LAKE setup (preloads LAKE bytecode + state).
;@include "intro/intro_transition_to_lake_setup.inc"

; Music-mark gates + the city-panning cinematic
; (`WAIT_MUS_MARK_2B_THEN_TEXT`, `SETUP_CITY_SEQ_CHANNELS`,
; `CITY_PAN_X_M2_Y_P1_6X`, etc.). The CITY_PAN_X_*_Y_*_NX labels
; are parameterised pan steps (delta-x, delta-y, repeat count); each
; runs a few frames then chains to the next pan delta. Music marks
; INTRO music-mark sync + city pan-shots (WAIT_MUS_MARK_2B et al.).
;@include "intro/intro_music_marks_and_city_pans.inc"

; City-sequence draw routines: DRAW_CITY_SEQ_432_433,
; DRAW_CITY_SEQ_435_436, DRAW_CITY_SEQ_439_440,
; INTRO_FILL_AND_DRAW_CIN_429_430, SETUP_INTRO_CITY_CHANNELS,
; the WAIT_*_BEFORE_COPY_PAGE_03 / DELAY_*_BEFORE_BLIT_DISPATCH
; cluster, plus DRAW_CIN_190_LOOP / DRAW_CIN_431_LOOP. The
; "draw routines" half of the city pan; corresponds to the
; per-frame video calls that the music_marks_and_city_pans
; INTRO city sequence: CIN_190 draw loop (alien-city establishing shots).
;@include "intro/intro_city_seq_draws.inc"

; Page-flip + on-screen-text helpers (`SHOW_PAGE_0_LOOP_INTRO`,
; `SHOW_PAGE_FF_LOOP_INTRO`, `SHOW_TEXT_39_AT_5_170_10X`). Used to
; display title-card text strings during pauses; the page-show
; loops alternate between drawing-page and visible-page so text
; INTRO page-show + on-screen text (SHOW_PAGE_0_LOOP_INTRO et al.).
;@include "intro/intro_page_show_and_text.inc"

; Song trigger + fade-in decor
; (`INTRO_PAUSE_3_PLAY_SONG_INIT`, `DELAY_50F_THEN_DRAW_CIN_454`,
; per-channel scene-decor inits `CH_03_INIT_VAR_01_02_FFF6`,
; `CH_04_INIT_VAR_04_05`, `CH_05_INIT_VAR_06_07`). Starts the
; main intro song and schedules the parallel decor draw loops
; INTRO song init + decor (INTRO_PAUSE_3_PLAY_SONG_INIT).
;@include "intro/intro_song_init_and_decor.inc"

; Late-phase variable-drift loops
; (`DRIFT_VAR1_PLUS_5_FOR_115X`, `DRIFT_VAR1_PLUS_4_FOR_25X`, ...).
; Long sequence of scripted parameter drifts that animate position
; offsets (`[VAR_01]`) for the lab-finale composition. Each label
; INTRO late-phase page fill (INIT_PAGE0_PAUSE2_FILL1 et al.).
;@include "intro/intro_late_pages_fill.inc"

; The actual LAKE-transition animation
; (`INTRO_TRANSITION_TO_LAKE_SCENE`, page-flip + palette-cycle
; loops `SELECT_PAGE0_AND_DISPATCH_BLIT`, `SELECT_PAGE_FF_LOOP`,
; the underwater pool reveal). Counterpart to
; `intro_transition_to_lake_setup.inc` — the setup chunk wires the
; INTRO lake-transition scene — the multi-phase cinematic that owns CH_02..CH_05 channel inits, the cinematic slide/rise/drift animations (SLIDE_CIN_448, RISE_CIN_447 / 130, DRAW_CIN_442..446 descending-Y phases, DRIFT_CIN_117 at five different positions), the city-seq channel setup, and the BLITTER_CYCLE that runs the page-flip during the transition. Largest INTRO chunk at 414 lines / 49 labels — kept whole because the scene flow is sequential.
;@include "intro/intro_lake_transition.inc"

; INTRO lake-phase visual FX (CIN_120 drift loop + particle drifts).
;@include "intro/intro_lake_phase_fx_drifts.inc"

; Late-intro parallax-scrolling phase
; (`PARALLAX_CIN_126_127_LOOP`, `ZOOM_OUT_VAR4_M3_LOOP`,
; `PARALLAX_REVERSE_3X`, `MUS_10_FORCE_KILL_CHANNELS`,
; `CH_05_INIT_VARS_06_07_08`). Drives the depth-illusion scrolling
; for the "view from the lab window" phase before the lightning
; INTRO scene-late-phase init (INIT_VAR_04_PAL_E_VAR_01).
;@include "intro/intro_scene_late_phase.inc"

; **First-to-execute scene** despite living last. The entry point
; in the first chunk schedules these onto channels 0x01/0x02/0x03:
;   ch 0x01 → `INTRO_SCENE_INIT_PARTICLES` (sets palette 1, draws
;             ~50 lab decor cinematics CIN_535..CIN_569, killChannel).
;   ch 0x02 → `INTRO_PLAY_BG_AUDIO_LOOP` (long sequential routine:
;             plays bg audio, draws the particle-accelerator
;             startup CIN_006..CIN_031, then jumps into
;             `DRAW_CIN_035_PAL_3_REPEAT_HEAD` in the DNA chunk).
;   ch 0x03 → `DRAW_CINEMATIC_005_LOOP` (looping avatar/idle draw).
; Also contains `INTRO_PLAY_FX_AND_PALETTE_4_LOOP` (Lester's walking-
; feet animation toward the lab door), `INTRO_FILL_AND_DRAW_CIN_103`
; (the city scene background), and the trailing-data label
; INTRO final scene: CIN_005 draw loop (transition into LAKE).
;@include "intro/intro_scene_final.inc"

; INTRO scene-final FX phase (palette + SFX loop).
;@include "intro/intro_scene_final_fx_phase.inc"
